  "title": "Titan's FY26 Target: Reverse-Engineer Growth via Goal Seek",
  "scenario": "You're a junior analyst on the Titan equity desk. Management guided FY26 EPS to ₹58, but the street consensus target demands EPS ₹62. Your model is built; now you must back-solve: what revenue CAGR (from FY25 base ₹8,400 cr) makes the numbers work? Use Goal Seek to answer — then audit the model for any buried hardcodes before shipping.",
  "instructions": "Audit the given Titan model using Ctrl+` and Go To Special, identify and eliminate any hardcoded plug, create a named range for the growth assumption, and use Goal Seek to find the revenue CAGR required to hit ₹62 EPS.",
  "learning_objective": "Audit an inherited model for buried numbers and inconsistencies, apply named ranges to load-bearing assumptions, and use Goal Seek to back-solve a key financial driver.",
  "hints": [
    "Ctrl+` will show you every formula at once — look for a typed number sitting alone in a column of formulas.",
    "Go To Special (F5 → Special → Constants) will highlight all hardcoded numbers — anything glowing outside the blue input section is suspect.",
    "Once you've cleaned the model, name the growth assumption cell (B4), then Goal Seek: Data → What-If → Goal Seek. Set cell = EPS (E11), To value = 62, By changing cell = the named growth input."
  ],
